IMPORT prelude

-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore) -- Part 2, the mediation gateway, and
-- the time limits in s 3(2) and s 3(3).
--
-- Nothing reaches the Employment Claims Tribunal except through this Part. s 3(1)
-- requires a mediation request before a claim is lodged; s 12(5) requires a
-- claim referral certificate for every dispute in the claim; and s 6 says when
-- the mediator must issue one. So the time limits here are the limitation
-- periods for every claim the Employment Act 1968, the Child Development
-- Co-Savings Act 2001 and the Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993 route to
-- this tribunal.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 1 April 2022, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ECA2016.txt
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules
-- skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human
-- gate.
--
-- NO REGULATIONS OR RULES OF COURT WERE RETRIEVED. The Act leaves to
-- regulations: which employees and employers may use the tribunal (s 12(2) and
-- (8)), the claim limits (s 12(7) and (8)(e)), the period for lodging after a
-- certificate issues (s 12(6)), the mediation fee, and the manner of
-- submission. Every one of those is carried here as a supplied fact or a
-- parameter. The figures commonly cited for the claim limits are NOT encoded,
-- because they are in regulations that were not read.

§ `Employment Claims Act 2016 -- Part 2 and the time limits`

§§ `2(1) -- the three kinds of dispute`

-- s 2(1): "'specified employment dispute' means a specified contractual dispute,
-- a specified statutory dispute or a wrongful dismissal dispute".
--
-- "specified contractual dispute" means "a dispute, relating to A PAYMENT OF AN
--   AMOUNT OF MONEY, which arises out of or in the course of employment under a
--   contract of service, about any matter specified in the First Schedule";
-- "specified statutory dispute" means "a dispute, relating to A PAYMENT OF AN
--   AMOUNT OF MONEY, about any matter specified in the Second Schedule".
--
-- Both definitions are confined to money. A dispute about anything else -- a
-- reference, a demotion, a transfer, a shift roster -- is not a specified
-- employment dispute however squarely it arises out of employment, and the
-- tribunal has no jurisdiction over it. The only non-money remedy anywhere in
-- the Act is reinstatement under s 12(3)(b), and that is available only on a
-- wrongful dismissal dispute.
DECLARE DisputeKind IS ONE OF
    `a specified contractual dispute`
    `a specified statutory dispute`
    `a wrongful dismissal dispute`
    `something else arising out of employment`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A DisputeKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this is a specified employment dispute` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `something else arising out of employment` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The First Schedule's eighteen items and the Second Schedule's are carried as
-- the three items that other sections single out, plus a catch-all. s 12(2)(c)
-- names First Schedule item 17 and Second Schedule items 14 and 16 as the only
-- matters an EMPLOYER may claim about; s 16(3) and (4) name First Schedule item
-- 17 and Second Schedule items 13 and 15 as the matters an employee loses by
-- going to the Minister.
DECLARE ScheduledMatter IS ONE OF
    `First Schedule item 17 -- salary in lieu of notice of termination`
    `Second Schedule item 13 -- the employee's entitlement under Employment Act section 11(1)`
    `Second Schedule item 14 -- the employer's entitlement under Employment Act section 11(1)`
    `Second Schedule item 15 -- the employee's entitlement under Employment Act section 16`
    `Second Schedule item 16 -- the employer's entitlement under Employment Act section 16`
    `some other matter in the First or Second Schedule`
    `no scheduled matter`

§§ `3(1) -- mediation first, always`

-- s 3(1): "BEFORE a claimant lodges a claim against a respondent, the claimant
-- must submit to the Commissioner a mediation request relating to EVERY
-- specified employment dispute for which the claim will be lodged."
--
-- Not "may". And "every" -- a claim that bundles four disputes needs all four
-- in the request.

§§ `3(2) -- when the request must be submitted`

-- The seven limbs, in the order the subsection gives them:
--
-- (a) recovery of salary under Employment Act 1968 s 65 -- within the s 65(2A)
--     period, or any period as extended under s 65(2B);
-- (b) a re-employment dispute described in Retirement and Re-employment Act
--     1993 s 8A(3) -- not later than 6 MONTHS after the last day of employment;
-- (c) a re-employment dispute under that Act's s 8B(7) -- within the time
--     determined under s 8B(8);
-- (d) a wrongful dismissal dispute for which an employee may lodge a claim under
--     Employment Act 1968 s 14(2) -- NOT LATER THAN ONE MONTH after the date of
--     the dismissal;
-- (e) a wrongful dismissal dispute for which a female employee may lodge a claim
--     under Employment Act 1968 s 84(2) -- within 2 MONTHS after the date of the
--     employee's confinement;
-- (f) any other specified employment dispute WHERE AN EMPLOYMENT RELATIONSHIP
--     HAS ENDED (by retirement, expiry, termination "or otherwise") -- not later
--     than 6 MONTHS after the last day of employment;
-- (g) any other specified employment dispute -- not later than ONE YEAR after
--     the date on which the material facts giving rise to THE EARLIEST specified
--     employment dispute listed in the mediation request occurred.
--
-- Limb (d) is the one most people meet: one month from dismissal to get a
-- mediation request in, for the central wrongful dismissal claim under the
-- Employment Act.
--
-- Limb (g) measures from the EARLIEST dispute in the request, not from each
-- dispute. Adding an old item to the list can therefore put the whole request
-- out of time -- though s 3(3)(a)(ii) would usually have stopped that item being
-- listed at all.
DECLARE RequestTiming HAS
    `the dispute is a recovery of salary under Employment Act section 65` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute is a re-employment dispute under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8A(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute is a re-employment dispute under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8B(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute under Employment Act section 14(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute under Employment Act section 84(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employment relationship has ended` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since the last day of employment` IS A NUMBER
    `months since the date of dismissal` IS A NUMBER
    `months since the date of confinement` IS A NUMBER
    `months since the material facts giving rise to the earliest dispute listed` IS A NUMBER
    `months since the material facts giving rise to this dispute` IS A NUMBER
    `within the period allowed by Employment Act section 65(2A), as extended if it was` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the time determined under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8B(8)` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Which limb governs. The limbs are ordered and exclusive: (f) is expressed as
-- "not being a dispute mentioned in paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e)", and
-- (g) is the residue.
DECLARE TimingLimb IS ONE OF
    `limb (a) -- salary under Employment Act section 65`
    `limb (b) -- re-employment under section 8A(3)`
    `limb (c) -- re-employment under section 8B(7)`
    `limb (d) -- wrongful dismissal under section 14(2)`
    `limb (e) -- wrongful dismissal under section 84(2)`
    `limb (f) -- the employment relationship has ended`
    `limb (g) -- anything else`

GIVEN `the timing` IS A RequestTiming
GIVETH A TimingLimb
DECIDE `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` IS
    IF   `the timing`'s `the dispute is a recovery of salary under Employment Act section 65`
    THEN `limb (a) -- salary under Employment Act section 65`
    ELSE IF   `the timing`'s `the dispute is a re-employment dispute under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8A(3)`
         THEN `limb (b) -- re-employment under section 8A(3)`
         ELSE IF   `the timing`'s `the dispute is a re-employment dispute under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8B(7)`
              THEN `limb (c) -- re-employment under section 8B(7)`
              ELSE IF   `the timing`'s `the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute under Employment Act section 14(2)`
                   THEN `limb (d) -- wrongful dismissal under section 14(2)`
                   ELSE IF   `the timing`'s `the dispute is a wrongful dismissal dispute under Employment Act section 84(2)`
                        THEN `limb (e) -- wrongful dismissal under section 84(2)`
                        ELSE IF   `the timing`'s `the employment relationship has ended`
                             THEN `limb (f) -- the employment relationship has ended`
                             ELSE `limb (g) -- anything else`

GIVEN `the timing` IS A RequestTiming
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request is in time under section 3(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the limb of section 3(2) that governs` `the timing`
    WHEN `limb (a) -- salary under Employment Act section 65`
        THEN `the timing`'s `within the period allowed by Employment Act section 65(2A), as extended if it was`
    WHEN `limb (b) -- re-employment under section 8A(3)`
        THEN `the timing`'s `months since the last day of employment` AT MOST 6
    WHEN `limb (c) -- re-employment under section 8B(7)`
        THEN `the timing`'s `within the time determined under Retirement and Re-employment Act section 8B(8)`
    WHEN `limb (d) -- wrongful dismissal under section 14(2)`
        THEN `the timing`'s `months since the date of dismissal` AT MOST 1
    WHEN `limb (e) -- wrongful dismissal under section 84(2)`
        THEN `the timing`'s `months since the date of confinement` AT MOST 2
    WHEN `limb (f) -- the employment relationship has ended`
        THEN `the timing`'s `months since the last day of employment` AT MOST 6
    OTHERWISE `the timing`'s `months since the material facts giving rise to the earliest dispute listed` AT MOST 12

§§ `3(3) -- what the request must and must not list`

-- s 3(3)(a): the request "must list every specified employment dispute in
-- relation to which ALL of the following requirements are satisfied at the time
-- the mediation request is submitted:
--   (i) if there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute, that claim
--       satisfies the requirements in section 12(2), (3) and (4);
--   (ii) THE MATERIAL FACTS GIVING RISE TO THE DISPUTE OCCURRED NOT EARLIER THAN
--        ONE YEAR BEFORE the date on which that request is submitted;
--   (iii) the dispute is not listed in an earlier mediation request between the
--         same parties already accepted by the Commissioner and not withdrawn
--         before the first mediation session under that earlier request."
--
-- s 3(3)(b) and (c) forbid listing a dispute in two further cases.
-- s 3(3)(d): the request must be accompanied by the prescribed fee.
--
-- SUB-PARAGRAPH (ii) IS A SECOND LIMITATION PERIOD, AND IT IS NOT THE SAME AS
-- THE ONE IN s 3(2). It runs from the material facts of the dispute itself, not
-- from the end of the employment, and it applies to every limb of s 3(2).
-- s 3(2)(f) gives six months from the last day of employment; s 3(3)(a)(ii)
-- still requires the facts to be under a year old. An employee owed an allowance
-- eighteen months ago who resigns today is inside s 3(2)(f) and outside
-- s 3(3)(a)(ii), and the dispute cannot be listed at all.
DECLARE ListingRequirements HAS
    `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that claim satisfies the requirements in section 12(2), (3) and (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the material facts occurred not earlier than one year before submission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute is listed in an earlier accepted request not withdrawn before its first session` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an earlier accepted request was required to list the dispute and the prescribed requirements are not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
    `under section 16 the claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the prescribed fee accompanied the request` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the requirements` IS A ListingRequirements
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(3)(a) requires this dispute to be listed` IF
         (NOT `the requirements`'s `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute`
          OR  `the requirements`'s `that claim satisfies the requirements in section 12(2), (3) and (4)`)
    AND `the requirements`'s `the material facts occurred not earlier than one year before submission`
    AND NOT `the requirements`'s `the dispute is listed in an earlier accepted request not withdrawn before its first session`

GIVEN `the requirements` IS A ListingRequirements
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3(3) forbids listing this dispute` IF
        `the requirements`'s `an earlier accepted request was required to list the dispute and the prescribed requirements are not satisfied`
    OR  (    `the requirements`'s `there is a claim for an amount relating to the dispute`
         AND `the requirements`'s `under section 16 the claim cannot be lodged with a tribunal`)

GIVEN `the requirements` IS A ListingRequirements
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` IF
        `section 3(3)(a) requires this dispute to be listed` `the requirements`
    AND NOT `section 3(3) forbids listing this dispute` `the requirements`

§§ `3(4) -- the Commissioner's power to refuse the request`

-- s 3(4)(a): the Commissioner "MAY refuse to accept a mediation request if --
--   (i) that request does not comply with the requirements in subsections (2)
--       and (3); or
--   (ii) the requirement in section 12(7) cannot be satisfied in relation to
--        that claim."
--
-- "May", not "must". Non-compliance does not void the request; it entitles the
-- Commissioner to refuse it. The encoding reports whether a ground to refuse
-- exists and does not decide the outcome, which is a discretion.
--
-- Limb (ii) brings the claim limits forward into the gateway: a request for an
-- amount above the prescribed limit can be refused before anyone reaches the
-- tribunal, which is where s 15's power to abandon the excess would have cured
-- it.
GIVEN `the timing` IS A RequestTiming,
      `the requirements` IS A ListingRequirements,
      `the total amount can satisfy the prescribed claim limits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner has a ground to refuse the request` IF
        NOT `the request is in time under section 3(2)` `the timing`
    OR  NOT `this dispute may be listed in the mediation request` `the requirements`
    OR  NOT `the requirements`'s `the prescribed fee accompanied the request`
    OR  NOT `the total amount can satisfy the prescribed claim limits`

-- s 3(5): "UPON ACCEPTING the mediation request, the Commissioner MUST, as soon
-- as reasonably practicable, refer every specified employment dispute listed in
-- that request for mediation by an approved mediator." Once accepted, the
-- referral is not discretionary.
GIVEN `the request was accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner must refer every listed dispute for mediation` IF
    `the request was accepted`

§§ `6 -- the claim referral certificate`

-- s 6(2): the mediator "MUST issue to the claimant a claim referral certificate
-- in respect of every unresolved specified employment dispute listed in the
-- mediation request, if --
--   (a) the respondent is given reasonable notice of, but does not attend, the
--       mediation for that dispute;
--   (b) no settlement is reached at the end of the mediation in relation to one
--       or more of the specified employment disputes listed; or
--   (c) the approved mediator is satisfied that there is no reasonable prospect
--       of settling through mediation."
--
-- s 6(3): "DESPITE SUBSECTION (2), if a claimant submits a mediation request
-- but, WITHOUT REASONABLE EXCUSE, FAILS TO ATTEND any mediation session to which
-- that request relates, the approved mediator MAY -- (a) discontinue the
-- mediation; and (b) refuse to issue to the claimant a claim referral
-- certificate".
--
-- s 6(4): a dispute is unresolved if it "(a) is not settled; and (b) is not
-- withdrawn from the list".
--
-- The asymmetry in s 6 is stark. A RESPONDENT who does not attend hands the
-- claimant a certificate under limb (a). A CLAIMANT who does not attend can be
-- refused one altogether -- and without a certificate for every dispute, s 12(5)
-- means no claim can be lodged. Read with the one-month limit in s 3(2)(d), a
-- claimant who misses the mediation session for a wrongful dismissal claim will
-- usually be out of time to begin again.
DECLARE MediationOutcome HAS
    `the respondent was given reasonable notice and did not attend` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no settlement was reached at the end of the mediation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute was settled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the dispute was withdrawn from the list` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant failed without reasonable excuse to attend a mediation session` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the mediator exercised the section 6(3) power to refuse a certificate` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A MediationOutcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dispute is unresolved within section 6(4)` IF
        NOT `the outcome`'s `the dispute was settled`
    AND NOT `the outcome`'s `the dispute was withdrawn from the list`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A MediationOutcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground in section 6(2) is made out` IF
        `the outcome`'s `the respondent was given reasonable notice and did not attend`
    OR  `the outcome`'s `no settlement was reached at the end of the mediation`
    OR  `the outcome`'s `the mediator is satisfied there is no reasonable prospect of settlement`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A MediationOutcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mediator may refuse a certificate under section 6(3)` IF
    `the outcome`'s `the claimant failed without reasonable excuse to attend a mediation session`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS A MediationOutcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mediator must issue a claim referral certificate` IF
        `the dispute is unresolved within section 6(4)` `the outcome`
    AND `a ground in section 6(2) is made out` `the outcome`
    AND NOT `the outcome`'s `the mediator exercised the section 6(3) power to refuse a certificate`

§§ `7 -- settlement, and the cap that follows it there`

-- s 7(1): where a dispute is settled at a mediation, the parties "MUST enter
-- into a settlement agreement in the form prescribed", it "must be signed by or
-- on behalf of each party", and the total payable to a party under it must not
-- exceed the SAME prescribed claim limits as s 12(7)(a) and (b).
--
-- So the claim limit binds a negotiated settlement as it binds an adjudicated
-- claim. Parties who agree a figure above the limit cannot record it in a
-- settlement agreement under this Part -- and s 15, which lets a claimant
-- abandon the excess before the tribunal, has no counterpart here.
--
-- s 7(2) and (3): a District Court may register the agreement, and once
-- registered it has the force of a District Court judgment and carries interest
-- as a judgment debt.
-- s 7(4) and (5): any party may apply within the prescribed period to set aside
-- the registration.
DECLARE Settlement HAS
    `a settlement agreement in the prescribed form was entered into` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was signed by or on behalf of each party` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total payable for contractual and statutory disputes is within the prescribed limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the total payable for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the prescribed limit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered in a District Court` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the settlement complies with section 7(1)` IF
        `the settlement`'s `a settlement agreement in the prescribed form was entered into`
    AND `the settlement`'s `it was signed by or on behalf of each party`
    AND `the settlement`'s `the total payable for contractual and statutory disputes is within the prescribed limit`
    AND `the settlement`'s `the total payable for wrongful dismissal disputes is within the prescribed limit`

GIVEN `the settlement` IS A Settlement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the settlement is enforceable as a District Court judgment` IF
    `the settlement`'s `registered in a District Court`

-- s 15 lets a claimant before the tribunal abandon an excess over the claim
-- limit. Nothing in s 7 lets parties at a mediation do the same.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a party at a mediation may abandon an excess over the claim limit` IF
    FALSE
